// Deal or Force - what each country is: its name, its colour on the map, and its capital.
//
// The capital is a city of the map: "capital_city" is its key in map_data/cities. The country
// is governed from the province under that city and its capital reads as that city's name
// (city.<key>.name) everywhere. "capital_name" beside a "capital_city" is only what the capital
// is called if the map has no such city: in one entry the city wins. A later file that gives
// "capital_name" alone renames the capital and keeps the city; "capital_latitude" and
// "capital_longitude" (optional) are the older way to place a capital, and a file that gives
// them without a city still works - the game finds the city standing there, even next door to
// the city named here.
//
// This is the definition. What a country *had* in 2024 - money, people, an army - is
// history/countries/2024/ instead, because those are edited by different people for
// different reasons and a total conversion usually wants one without the other.
//
// Every file in this folder is read in name order and later files win, so a mod that
// renames six countries ships `50_my_names.json` with six entries and inherits the
// rest. It never has to copy this file, and so never goes stale against it.
//
// Generated by Tools/MapDataCompiler. Edit it by hand if you like - nothing
// regenerates it unless the compiler is run.
